    rdfs:seeAlso <https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/294.html> ;
    skos:broader cwe:CWE-1390 ;
    skos:definition "A capture-replay flaw exists when the design of the product makes it possible for a malicious user to sniff network traffic and bypass authentication by replaying it to the server in question to the same effect as the original message (or with minor changes)."@en ;
